  "$comment": "Astrology vocabulary the grounding validator gates on (SPEC §5.3 step 9). A sentence is an ASTROLOGICAL CLAIM — and must cite a fact-ID present in the served payload — when it contains a STRONG term, or a WEAK term together with a number. The split exists to keep the validator honest in both directions: 'Saturn is in your 10th' must be caught, and 'I don't have your birth chart yet' must not be, or Tara could never say the one sentence §5.3 most wants her to say. Graha / rashi / nakshatra / choghadiya / paksha names are NOT listed here — they are derived from the sitara_schemas enums at import time and are always strong, so the lexicon cannot drift from the engine.",
