  "ordinal_house_patterns": {
    "$comment": "An ordinal next to a house word is always a claim — '3 things to do' is not. Each pattern's group(1) is the ordinal TOKEN, digits or word; `ordinal_house_words` maps the word forms back to a number so the §5.3 numbers-verbatim check still runs. Hindi and Hinglish carry word forms because that is what the §7.1 brief templates render (पहले भाव, never 1वें).",
    "en": "\\b(\\d{1,2})(?:st|nd|rd|th)\\s+house\\b",
    "hi": "((?:\\d{1,2}\\s*(?:वें|वाँ|वा)?)|ग्यारहवें|ग्यारहवाँ|पाँचवें|पाँचवाँ|पांचवें|पांचवाँ|बारहवें|बारहवाँ|सातवें|सातवाँ|दूसरे|दूसरा|तीसरे|तीसरा|आठवें|आठवाँ|नौवें|नौवाँ|दसवें|दसवाँ|पहले|पहला|चौथे|चौथा|छठे|छठा)\\s*भाव",
    "hi-Latn": "\\b((?:\\d{1,2}(?:st|nd|rd|th|ve|vein|va|vaan)?)|paanchve|gyarahve|chauthe|chautha|panchve|chhathe|barahve|doosre|doosra|teesre|teesra|chhata|saatve|saatva|aathve|aathva|pehle|pehla|dusre|nauve|nauva|dasve|dasva)\\s*(?:house|bhaav|bhav)\\b"
  },
  "$exemption_comment": "A sentence carrying a STRONG term is exempt from citation only when ALL FIVE hold: no number, no clock value, no second-person reference, no temporal deixis, and no celestial entity asserted to be doing or being anything. That last clause is why `celestial` and `state_motion` exist. Category terms (choghadiya, muhurat, tithi, rahu kaal as CONCEPTS) may be glossed uncited — §2.3 requires that gloss — but a named body is never uncited. Devanagari and Hinglish celestial names are listed per locale because the sitara_schemas enums are English identifiers only; without them 'शुक्र वक्री है' would slip through the exemption it is meant to fail.",
  "celestial": {
    "$comment": "Named bodies and points, keyed by the CANONICAL enum id so a surface form resolves to the body it names. English is derived from the Graha/Rashi/Nakshatra enums at import; these are the locale renderings the enums cannot supply. Restructured from a flat list in M8-P10: the flat form could say a sentence NAMES a body but not WHICH, so the grounding validator could not tell 'Venus is in your 10th house' citing Saturn's fact from the truth. `_celestial_surface_map` inverts this; the flat set the marker net wants is the values flattened, so there is still one source.",
